+their existing behavior. This example does not cover additional data formats or external tuning libraries.
+
+#### Inspect the selected training parameters
+
+Newly fitted tuning models retain a textual snapshot of the final estimator's training configuration.
+`getBestModelInfo()` includes separately labelled trainer and estimator sections, with the owning class and UID.
+It reports training-only settings such as LightGBM's `numLeaves` even when the fitted prediction model does not
+expose them as mutable parameters. Fields are sorted and scalar values use JSON encoding; complex objects and
+binary training buffers are represented by placeholders rather than embedded in the report.
+Where legacy fitted-model details are renderable, a `model:` section retains their original formatting;
+a non-fatal formatting failure is represented by `<unrenderable>` instead of failing training.
+The JSON encoding and other placeholder rules apply to the new trainer and estimator sections.
+
+The snapshot is copied and saved with the tuning model. `getBestModelParamsInfo()` reads that informational
+field directly; manually changing the field also changes the reported provenance.
+For classification and regression, the snapshot is recorded only when the selected estimator inherits Spark's
+standard `fit(dataset, paramMap)` implementation. Custom overrides retain their original fit dispatch and
+legacy reporting. Models saved without a snapshot also retain their legacy reporting, including the unsupported
+model-type error for legacy ranker models. Newly fitted ranker models support the report.
+Models saved with the new field may not be readable by earlier releases.
+
+The following synthetic example selects a non-default leaf limit and reads it through the Python API:
+
+<!--pytest-codeblocks:cont-->
+```python
+from pyspark.sql import SparkSession
+from synapse.ml.automl import TuneHyperparameters
+from synapse.ml.automl.HyperparamBuilder import (
+    DiscreteHyperParam,
+    HyperparamBuilder,
+    RandomSpace,
+)
+from synapse.ml.lightgbm import LightGBMClassifier
+from synapse.ml.train import TrainClassifier
+
+info_spark = SparkSession.builder.getOrCreate()
+info_data = info_spark.range(64).selectExpr(
+    "cast(id % 8 - 4 as double) as x", "cast(id % 8 >= 4 as double) as label"
+)
+info_learner = LightGBMClassifier(
+    numIterations=2, minDataInLeaf=1, numTasks=1, numThreads=1, verbosity=-1
+)
+info_trainer = TrainClassifier(model=info_learner, labelCol="label", inputCols=["x"])
+info_space = HyperparamBuilder().addHyperparam(
+    info_learner, info_learner.numLeaves, DiscreteHyperParam([7])
+)
+info_best = TuneHyperparameters(
+    models=[info_trainer],
+    evaluationMetric="accuracy",
+    numFolds=2,
+    numRuns=1,
+    parallelism=1,
+    paramSpace=RandomSpace(info_space.build()).space(),
+    seed=7,
+).fit(info_data)
+assert "numLeaves: 7" in info_best.getBestModelInfo()
+```
